  "feedbacks": [],
  "notes": [
    "The module has no feedbacks (grandma2.js only sets action definitions and one variable, response).",
    "Transport: Telnet to the console (port 30000), login with user and password from the module config; every action sends a command line (command, or LUA 'gma.canbus.*' calls). The module text names the console; the manifest lists only GrandMA2 and does not mention onPC or other variants, so onPC coverage is not verified.",
    "The button option 'button' has the numeric default 11 while all choice ids are strings ('11'); the catalog records the source as written (actions.js:38-41, choices.js).",
    "The encoder and encoder_p actions are built in a block after the literal action table (actionDefs[cmd]); the option list is the shared encOpt array (checkbox, dropdown, textinput) followed by the action-specific options. The enc dropdown ids are numbers 0-7 (ar2obj in actions.js:3-5); labels read 'Main Encoder (1)' to 'Screen 4 Encoder (8)'.",
    "Encoder fields: when encoder_from_variable is checked, encoder_variable (1-8, variables allowed) replaces enc; the callback clamps it to 0-7 after subtracting 1.",
    "Legacy action ids pushbutton, relbutton and encoder<N> exist only in upgrade scripts (upgrades.js) and are not registered actions.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ^1.8.0: no expressions; variables only through useVariables text inputs."
  ]
